@meta
id: 26-05
title: Drill — filter the paragraph
chapter: 26
type: drill
skills: filter-bang
par: 19
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: select the block, retype it in order, delete the repeats
open: migration-notes.txt

@brief
Eight times: sort the block of table names at the top and drop the
repeats, without looking at a single line number. Leave the sentence
below the blank line alone.

@keys
| `!ip` | filter the paragraph under the cursor |
| `sort -u` | sorted, one of each |

@hints
The cursor already starts in the block, so the paragraph object covers
exactly the lines you want.
--
`!ip` then `sort -u` then Enter.

@solution
    !ip sort -u<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Fifteen keystrokes and no counting. The reason to drill the object form
rather than the range form is that the object form does not care where
the block is or how long it is, so it survives the block growing by four
lines next week — and a filter applied to the wrong range is a worse
mistake than most, because the command rewrites everything it is handed.

@start migration-notes.txt
orders
customers
payments
orders
refunds
customers
invoices

Every table above is locked for the duration of the migration.

@expected migration-notes.txt
customers
invoices
orders
payments
refunds

Every table above is locked for the duration of the migration.
